# Fresh BRK demo implementations

When implementing or discussing BRK-* work in Barkenciaga:

## Source of truth

- Current `main` and the Jira ticket (acceptance criteria, description)
- In-repo demo docs on `main`: `DEMO_SCRIPTS.md`, `TECH_DEBT.md`, seeded teaching bugs

## Do not restore prior implementations

- Do not fetch closed PR refs (`git fetch origin pull/<n>/head`, `refs/pull/*`)
- Do not checkout, cherry-pick, merge, or diff against commits from closed PRs or deleted branches
- Do not use `gh pr view`, `gh pr diff`, or GitHub PR pages to copy prior BRK solution code
- Do not pull implementation details from old Cursor plans or prior agent sessions

Known closed PRs (BRK-1, BRK-2, BRK-4, BRK-6, BRK-10, etc.) are **discarded demo history**, not templates.

## Workflow

1. Confirm you are on up-to-date `main`
2. Create a new branch for the ticket
3. Implement from Jira + existing `main` patterns only

Only restore a specific closed PR if the user explicitly requests it by PR number or commit SHA.
